---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import PixelField from "../components/PixelField.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — DataDoodles"
  description="DataDoodles rebuilds SME websites in Malaysia and Singapore so they get found in Google and in AI search — ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and AI Overviews. Rigorous data, drawn by hand."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main>
    <section class="section about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <PixelField />
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span>About DataDoodles</span></p>
        <h1 id="about-title">Rigorous data, drawn by hand.</h1>
        <p class="about-lede">
          Data is the substance. Doodles are the delivery. We're serious about outcomes, unserious about ourselves.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="about-what-title">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            DataDoodles rebuilds Malaysian and Singaporean SME websites so they get found in Google <em>and</em> in
            AI search — ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, and Google's AI Overview. Most business websites were built for
            a search engine that ranks ten blue links. That engine is no longer the only one that matters: AI models
            now answer a question directly, naming one business, maybe three. No page two.
          </p>

          <h2>Who we work with</h2>
          <p>
            Clinics, law firms, professional services, education providers, and specialist trades in the Klang
            Valley and across Singapore — established businesses that already have customers and reviews, and a
            website that reflects neither. Typically RM500k–RM10m in revenue, run by owners who are busy running
            the business, not managing a website.
          </p>

          <h2>Why the name</h2>
          <p>
            The underlying page is a precision instrument: schema markup, entity structure, page speed, semantic
            HTML — the unglamorous technical work that determines whether an AI model can understand and cite a
            business at all. The "doodle" is what sits on top of that: a hand-drawn mark circling the moment your
            business gets named in an AI answer, the same way a consultant marks up a report in front of you.
            Rigorous underneath. Legible on the surface.
          </p>

          <h2>How we work</h2>
          <p>
            We publish our prices. We refuse to guarantee rankings — anyone who does is guessing. And we turn away
            businesses that aren't a good fit rather than take the engagement anyway. The typical project runs
            about 30 days from kickoff to a before-and-after report: what each AI platform said about your business
            before we started, and what it says now.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="about-cta-title">
      <div class="shell about-cta">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span>See it in detail</span></p>
        <h2 id="about-cta-title">See what happened for businesses like yours.</h2>
        <a class="hero-cta" href="/case-study">
          See the case studies <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    max-width: 16ch;
    margin-top: var(--s5);
  }

  .about-lede {
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin-top: var(--s5);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-cta {
    max-width: 60ch;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .about-cta h2 {
    max-width: 20ch;
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }

  .about-cta .hero-cta {
    margin-top: var(--s6);
  }
</style>
